      ],
      "source": "https://ohmyfacts.com/world/cities/30-facts-about-peoria/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1942, a moldy cantaloupe in a Peoria grocery store yielded the first industrial penicillin strain, Penicillium chrysogenum.",
